Viewer: fixes from the F50 drive of 2026-10-13 (XPeng, Chrome 120, wireless CarPlay), most tried in the car the
same evening by swapping the page over Tailscale.

Media card: the car's card reads only the Media Session position state and runs it on by its own clock, which put
the bar at the end all the time (without a position state it showed no bar; with the music element on the song's
timeline the bar still stood full). The position now goes out on every 750 ms tick at a near-zero rate (0 is
refused): the bar follows the song. Its play/pause state follows the iPhone's own.

Music keeps its own timeline again. Moving the element onto the song (playport-media-element-timeline,
playport-music-seamless-align) seeked on every song change, a short hiccup each time; when the next song was
shorter Chrome 120 removed buffered audio on the smaller duration, so the next appendBuffer threw "This
SourceBuffer is still processing" into the error banner; and while the iPhone's now-playing reports stalled over
Bluetooth (93 s without one) it pulled the music back every 5 s. How far behind the newest audio it plays is
logged (musicLeadMaxMs/MinMs, 0.8 to 1.5 s), not drained by playing faster: 1.03x crackled at song changes.

The car pauses the iPhone over its Bluetooth for its own video app and does not resume it; the page plays on the
iPhone's silence, so the car turns its play/pause key into pause. A pause key while the iPhone is paused now means
play: one press of the steering wheel or the card plays again. (Pausing the element with the iPhone instead made
the car's video app fall silent after a second or two.)

Fullscreen: #app is pinned to the window's edges instead of 100dvh, which Chrome 120 left at 641 px after
fullscreen changes while the window was 579, so CarPlay's bottom row (home button) went below the screen; the
renegotiations to 1280x936 came from that same stale height. Fullscreen is renegotiated once per browser, not on
every entry, a close shape only stretching. A tap goes back to fullscreen only after the car covered the page
(reverse camera), not in the 2 s after leaving fullscreen with the car's back button, when it never reached
CarPlay.

Calls (same evening, iPhone not on the car's own Bluetooth): the other side heard crackle. Opus input streams
count their RTP timestamps in the stream's own rate, 16 kHz for telephony and 24 kHz for Siri (audioFormat bits),
while every 20 ms packet advanced them by 960 (48 kHz); now 320 and 480 (MicrophoneConfig.clockRate), and the
call was heard. The XPeng's microphone reaches the browser very quiet (speech peaking at 1% of full scale), so the
page raises it 16 times with a limiter (?micgain=1..64), the owner's choice: the voice is heard best, though the
other side also hears the echo of the car's speakers the browser leaves (open). Ducking the microphone while the
far end played did not remove it and made the voice rough, so it is not used.

For the next drive's log: the page build, the window/viewport/screen sizes with each page event (ev 5 on resize),
the car's media keys that reached the page (keyPlay/keyPause/keyPauseAsPlay/keyNext/keyPrev), play() refused by
the browser (musicBlocked), the microphone (micState/micPackets/micFrames/micPeak/micGain, mic context, track
and encoder), the far end's queue and output latency (farQueueMaxMs/outLatMs), and each media key the receiver sends to the iPhone ("viewer media key").

